Jonker wrote:

> (spoiler i guess)
> 
> do you normally call your dog Bonafido?
> if so, then it was a "bones" dog..
> in other words, yes a reincarnation.
> sometimes the bones dogs come back with ghosts of
> previous characters you played, sometimes not. I'm not
> sure if there's a difference between pets that died in previous
> games or ones that were just abandoned (by your death
> or otherwise).
> 
The only times when a pet from a previous game turns up not accompanied by 
a ghost are when they turn up accompanied by some other manifestation of a 
previous character (e.g. a mummy)---they don't turn up on their own. Nor 
do the pets turn up if they died, only if the player accompanying them 
died. Abandoned pets will only turn up if they were on the same level as 
the player when the player died, but their status as pets or former pets 
doesn't matter when you meet them: they are just creatures with names at 
that point.

Of course, what can happen quite easily is that pets fall down trapdoors or 
step on level teleport traps, so you could meet an expet on a level which 
isn't a bones level, but only after you have visited the bones level it 
came from.


